'''WED-15-ST68''' was an ancient [[WED-15 Septoid Treadwell]] owned by a [[Nebit's tribe|clan]] of [[Jawa]]s on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]]. In [[1 BBY]], the Jawa's stopped their sandcrawler stopped at the [[Lars homestead|Lars Homestead]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] in order to sell [[droid]]s to the [[Lars family]], but the [[moisture farmer]] [[Owen Lars]] had no interest in purchasing WED-15-ST68. After leaving the homestead, the Jawa sandcrawler was attacked by [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[stormtrooper]]s who [[Death|destroyed]] WED-15-ST68.

==Biography==
WED-15-ST68<ref name="ANHStory">''[[Star Wars « Episode 4 Story »]]''</ref> was a [[WED-15 Septoid Treadwell]] manufactured by [[Cybot Galactica]].<ref name="BR2D2" /> By [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> WED-15-ST68 was ancient<ref name="BR2D2" /> and was one of 1,500 [[droid]]s<ref name="ANHStory" /> that a [[Nebit's tribe|tribe]] of [[Jawa]] [[scavenger]]s led by the [[chief]]tain [[Nebit]]<ref name="Nebit">{{ForceCollection|Nebit|star=3}}</ref> kept in their [[sandcrawler]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]]. While owned by the Jawas, it was likely that WED-15-ST68 was enhanced by the scavengers, possibly through augmentation of its original manipulator [[Limb|arms]] with others that the Jawas had lying about.<ref name="Encyclopedia" />

In 1 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> the sandcrawler stopped at the [[Lars homestead|Lars Homestead]] in the [[Jundland Wastes]] of Tatooine so that the Jawas could present droids to the [[Lars family]] for sale. Hoping to finally get rid of WED-15-ST68,<ref name="BR2D2" /> the Jawas included it in a line up of droids for the family to browse, with a pair of Jawas escorting the [[WED Treadwell repair droid]] down the sandcrawler's ramp.<ref name="Vehicles">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref> However, [[moisture farmer]] [[Owen Lars]] showed no interest in WED-15-ST68<ref name="BR2D2" /> and instantly dismissed it,<ref name="ANH" /> as the family already owned the [[WED-15-XT Treadwell droid]] [[WED-15-77]] who had a smaller base that gave it more maneuverability and allowed it to move in closer to machinery for delicate work with smaller more delicate [[Limb|arms]].<ref name="BR2D2" />

After the moisture farmers ultimately chose to purchase the [[droid]]s [[C-3PO]] and [[R2-D2]], several Jawas crowded around WED-15-ST68<ref name="ANH" /> before it and the other droids were moved back into the sandcrawler.<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> Nebit's tribe was latter attacked by [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[stormtrooper]]s who were searching for the two droids that had been sold.<ref name="ANH" /> The [[trooper]]s [[Death|killed]] the Jawas on board the sandcrawler and destroyed WED-15-ST68,<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> leaving the damaged sandcrawler and its slaughtered occupants abandoned in the [[desert]].<ref name="ANH" />

==Characteristics==
Standing one [[meter]] in height,<ref name="Databank" /> WED-15-ST68 was equipped with seven<ref name="ANH" /> multiple jointed arms that made it look like a giant [[spider]].<ref name="ANHAudio">{{Film|IV}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> The [[Maintenance droid|repair droid]] had [[Color|black]], multi-range [[photoreceptor]]s and was also equipped with a communications [[antenna]], which connected to a bracket on the droid's base near its logic housing. WED-15-ST68 was primarily white in color but had two raised orange areas on its base.<ref name="Encyclopedia" />

